nd EN 50163:2004: clause 4\\\" ;\\n                       vs:term_status \\\"stable\\\" ;\\n                       skos:editorialNote \\\"Present and unchanged since <http://data.europa.eu/eli/dec_impl/2011/665>\\\"@en ;\\n                       skos:scopeNote \\\"\\\"\\\"If the real values exceed range of the EN 50163:2004+A1:2007+A2:2020+A3:2022, they could be introduced by the Agency on request via a process of change request.\\nSee: ENE TSI: 4.2.3 and EN 50163:2004: clause 4\\n\\nFor RINF XML data sets:\\nAs long as the data provision through XML data sets is allowed, an XML attribute called “Set” will be used to link the value of this parameter to the parameter 1.1.1.2.2.1.1 / ECS_SystemType\\\"\\\"\\\"@en .\\n\\n\", \"source_date_note\": \"La cabecera declara issued 2024-04-18; la versión y fecha de cada término se conservan en el bloque\", \"version\": \"v3.3.4\", \"year\": null}, \"EI_EI-18\": {\"author\": \"Ghislain Atemezing; Maarten Duhoux; Dragos Patru\", \"kind\": \"Ontología externa; fuente semántica, sin adopción normativa colombiana\", \"locator\": \"http://data.europa.eu/949/maximumPermittedSpeed; línea 12815\", \"path\": \"Biblioteca_ontologias_transporte/20260908/originales/ERA/ontology.ttl\", \"publisher\": \"European Union Agency for Railways\", \"sha256\": \"9081264e5059029ec91cc5fab7f310cc4d764788f9d37f330504e4955e6de289\", \"source_block\": \"###  http://data.europa.eu/949/maximumPermittedSpeed\\nera:maximumPermittedSpeed rdf:type owl:DatatypeProperty ;\\n                          rdfs:subPropertyOf era:performanceDataParameter ;\\n                          rdf:type owl:FunctionalProperty ;\\n                          rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;\\n                                        owl:unionOf ( era:CommonCharacteristicsSubset\\n                                                      era:RunningTrack\\n                                                    )\\n                                      ] ;\\n                          rdfs:range xsd:integer ;\\n                          era:XMLName \\\"IPP_MaxSpeed\\\" ;\\n                          era:applicable \\\"Y/N\\\" ;\\n                          era:legalDeadline \\\"In accordance with Implementing Decision 2014/880/EU and by 16 March 2019 at the latest\\\"@en ;\\n                          era:rinfIndex \\\"1.1.1.1.2.5\\\" ;\\n                          era:shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/MaximumPermittedSpeed> ;\\n                          era:tsiOPEAppendixD2Index \\\"3.1.4\\\" ;\\n                          era:unitOfMeasure unit:KiloM-PER-HR ;\\n                          era:usedInRCCCalculations \\\"true\\\"^^xsd:boolean ;\\n                          dcterms:created \\\"2020-08-24\\\"^^xsd:date ;\\n                          dcterms:modified \\\"2023-03-14\\\"^^xsd:date ,\\n                                           \\\"2024-09-19\\\"^^xsd:date ,\\n                                           \\\"2025-02-26\\\"^^xsd:date ;\\n                          rdfs:comment \\\"Nominal maximum operational speed on the line as a result of infrastructure, energy and control, command signalling subsystem characteristics expressed in kilometres/hour.\\\"@en ;\\n                          rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;\\n                          rdfs:label \\\"Maximum permitted speed\\\"@en ;\\n                          rdfs:seeAlso \\\"INF TSI, ENE TSI, CCS TSI\\\" ;\\n                          vs:term_status \\\"stable\\\" ;\\n                          skos:example \\\"\\\"\\\"In case INF, ENE and/or CCS allow different speeds, the max permitted speed on this track of this section of line shall be the lowest one.\\nIn case the maximum permitted speed for freight and passenger trains operation are different, the max permitted speed on this track of this section of line shall be the highest one.\\\"\\\"\\\" ;\\n                          skos:scopeNote \\\"\\\\\\\"Speed on the line\\\\\\\" shall be understood as spee